const tests = done('tests:' + K) || await agent(RULES + '\nRole: test writer (Engineer), rules.md section (d), for ' + ROW + ': ' + SPEC + '. Branch ' + TB + ', suffix vg-harness-' + K + '-tests, from origin/main. You create ONLY ' + NEWTEST + ' (new; it imports the helpers of tests/specfactory/test_spec_provenance.py and, for T12, tests/specfactory/test_pre_gate.py with sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent)) as test_pre_gate.py does, and edits neither). Tests are the spec: write the cases below, one per sentence of the brief and of IFACE, with the exact fixtures and expected lines IFACE gives. You are NOT the builder. The file header quotes the brief\'s four test sentences word for word (method rev 3) and states the UNSTATED INTERFACES you had to assume (the usage text, the order of the PROVSCOPE fields is fixed by IFACE item 5).\n' + BRIEF + '\n' + IFACE + '\n' + RULED + '\n' + WHOLE + '\nThe file carries a line "# Rule pins: <ids>" in its first 40 lines; this piece proves no bible rule, so write "# Rule pins: none (tooling piece, Architect derivation brief 2026-10-21)".\nCASES (pytest, subprocess with sys.executable, the fixture of IFACE item 8): (T1) the clean id passes: --pieces VG-X-clean exits 0, prints no finding line, and prints the PROVSCOPE line with paragraphs=1 in-scope=0 whole-file=2; (T2) the dirty id rejects: --pieces VG-X-dirty exits 1, prints exactly one finding line at the dirty paragraph\'s line with "(1)", and the PROVSCOPE line with in-scope=1 whole-file=2; (T3) both ids: exit 1, one finding (the dirty one), paragraphs=2; (T4) the whole-file count is information: the VG-X-other finding is never printed with --pieces VG-X-clean or VG-X-dirty, yet whole-file=2 says it exists; (T5) no match [R3b]: --pieces VG-X-nothing prints both findings, exits 1, paragraphs=0 in-scope=2 whole-file=2, and NO WARN line; (T5b) the WARN line [R3b]: --pieces VG-X-clean,VG-X-ghost,VG-X-dirty,VG-X-ghost exits 1 and prints, after the PROVSCOPE line, exactly one line `PROVSCOPE WARN <path> id=VG-X-ghost opens no paragraph` (the repeated id once, no WARN for the two ids that matched); --pieces VG-X-clean,VG-X-ghost exits 0 (a WARN never changes the exit code); (T6) the cited-number rule [R2] on small fixtures (a [W Q-990-01: "soon"] tag then the number, same unit unless stated), in BOTH modes (one-argument and --pieces with an id that opens nothing): "the delay is 3 s [P csrc/x.c:12]" passes (exit 0, no (10)); "the delay is 3 s. See [P csrc/x.c:12]" passes (the cite is in another sentence of the same unit); "see [P csrc/x.c:12] the delay is 3 s" passes (the cite is in the opening tag run BEFORE the number); "the delay is 3 s [P csrc/x.c]" gives (10) number 3 (no line; today it also gives the (3) finding for the missing line, which stays); a number in one blank-separated paragraph and the [P csrc/x.c:12] cite in the NEXT paragraph gives (10) number 3 at the first paragraph\'s line; the same with the cite in the next LIST ITEM unit gives (10) number 3; a cite does not clear reasons 3, 8 or 9 (the "[P csrc/x.c]" case keeps its (3)); (T7) the list-item openings [DRAFT-provscope-forms]: a fixture of adjacent lines "- `VG-X-item`: The tile shows 5 wu of rubble when asked.", "- `VG-X-next`: The tile shows 5 wu of rubble when asked. [W Q-990-01]" "- VG-X-plain (note): The tile shows 5 wu of rubble when asked." and a bare "- VG-X-bare" line followed by the continuation line "  The tile shows 5 wu of rubble when asked.": --pieces VG-X-item rejects at its own line, --pieces VG-X-next passes (the range of the list-item forms ends at the next list item), --pieces VG-X-plain rejects at its own line (the plain `- ID` form with an open parenthesis as follower), --pieces VG-X-bare rejects at the continuation line (end of line is a follower of the plain `- ID` form: a bare `- ID` line opens a paragraph); a bullet that only mentions an id ("- see VG-X-item for the rubble") opens nothing; (T8) the bold opening is exactly the paragraph\'s rule [DRAFT-provscope-forms]: with paragraphs opening **VG-X-dirty (lane X; Tool: Workflow).**, **VG-X-dirty-more (lane X).** and **VG-X-two, VG-X-three (lane X).** (each with an untagged behaviour sentence): --pieces VG-X-dirty names only the first (the character after the id in the second is `-`, not a space, a comma or an open parenthesis), --pieces VG-X-dir (a prefix) names none, --pieces VG-X-two names the third (a comma follows the id) and --pieces VG-X-three names NONE (a second id inside a bold opening is a mention, not an opening: the widening of the first draft is gone, so this is the negative control), a paragraph opening **VG-X-dot.** (a full stop follows the id) is named by no id, an id named only after the closing ** or in the body opens nothing, and a line with text before the ** opens nothing; (T9) the range: a paragraph of two adjacent lines (the bold line, then a list-item line holding an untagged behaviour sentence) scoped by its id reports the finding on the second line; the next blank-separated paragraph\'s finding is outside; a heading line right after the paragraph ends it; (T10) usage: --pieces without a value, an unknown option and two spec arguments exit 2 with a usage line on stderr; (T11) POSITIVE CONTROLS, green today on the base tree: one-argument mode on the fixture exits 1 with exactly the two reason-1 findings and NO PROVSCOPE line (today\'s whole-file mode rejects both ids\' paragraphs by rejecting the file), the same mode on a fixture of the clean paragraph alone exits 0 with empty stdout (the detector is not always-failing), and the existing tests/specfactory/test_spec_provenance.py reason 10 case `[W Q-990-01: "soon"] the delay is 3 s` still gives (10) with no cite; (T12) ' + (PREGATE_EDIT ? 'through pre_gate.sh [R1]: in a throwaway repo (_make_repo, _stub_gate, _pieces, _run, EPICS of test_pre_gate.py) with the fixture as spec.md and rows VG-X-clean and VG-X-dirty both carrying spec = "spec.md": pre_gate.sh with the piece list "VG-X-clean" prints PRE_GATE provenance OK for spec.md and ends PRE_GATE verdict OK, with "VG-X-dirty" prints PRE_GATE provenance REJECT and ends PRE_GATE verdict REJECT; with the list "VG-X-clean,VG-X-ghost" the output carries the PROVSCOPE WARN line for VG-X-ghost and the verdict stays OK (a row VG-X-ghost without a spec key adds its own "no spec key" WARN: expected); and the control green today: PRE_GATE_SPEC=spec.md (the extra path) with the piece list "P-1" (no id opens a paragraph) rejects the same fixture whole-file. You do NOT edit test_pre_gate.py; its :252 and :370 cases stay green.' : 'through pre_gate.sh: args.pregate is false, so the ids do not reach the lint: write only the control green today (PRE_GATE_SPEC=spec.md rejects the fixture whole-file) and say in the report that T12 is dormant.') + ' (T14) the empty list (independent of args.pregate): `--pieces ""` exits 1 on the fixture with both reason-1 findings and the line `PROVSCOPE <path> pieces= paragraphs=0 in-scope=2 whole-file=2`, on the clean-only fixture exits 0 with `pieces= paragraphs=0 in-scope=0 whole-file=0`. Then the RED cases, red for the stated reason: today ' + LINT + ' accepts exactly one argument, so every --pieces case exits 2 with its usage line (paste what python reports); the cited-number cases that now pass (first three of T6 and the same-unit ones) exit 1 with a (10) finding on the base tree; T1 to T10, T12 and those T6 cases fail on those reasons, and every control of T11 and the "no cite stays a finding" T6 cases are green. Thresholds: none invented; every number is a fixture value, cited.\n' + BL + '\nON THE BUILT TREE (the base, no feature): run ' + NEWTEST + ' and tests/specfactory once; the new cases must be red for the reasons above (paste the failing assertion line of EVERY red test verbatim: file:line and message) and every control green (paste the pytest summary line). Pre-gate: ' + PREGATE('<worktree>', 'origin/main', NEWTEST) + '; red tests make the test step REJECT by design: quote that line and say the other steps are OK. Report ok, branch, sha, summary (failing lines, control lines, the fixture line numbers), red_ids.', { label: 'tests:' + K, phase: 'Tests', schema: REPORT, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' })
out = { ...out, tests }
if (!(tests && tests.ok)) return { ...out, stopped: 'tests:' + K }

phase('Build')
const mkBuild = (extra) => done('build:' + K) || agent(RULES + '\nRole: Doer (rules.md section (a)) for ' + ROW + ': ' + SPEC + '. Branch ' + BB + ', suffix vg-harness-' + K + ', from origin/main; merge origin/' + tests.branch + rulingMerge() + extra + '.\nEdit ONLY ' + PRODUCT + ' (the owner row ' + ROW + ' also owns ' + NEWTEST + ': that is the test writer\'s, you never edit it' + (PREGATE_EDIT ? '; in ' + PREGATE_SH + ' change only the spec_provenance.py call line at step (5) provenance (located by its text, IFACE item 2): no dedupe of repeated spec paths and no header-comment edit; ' + TESTPG + ' is NOT yours' : '; ' + PREGATE_SH + ' is NOT in your list') + '). Build exactly the INTERFACE: every option, pattern, output field and rule it names. Numbers: this piece has none beyond the fixtures; a rule IFACE and the rulings do not give stops you with stop_reason "spec-gap: <what>". Keep one-argument mode byte for byte as today. Comments only where non-obvious: the two DRAFT names of IFACE item 7 and, where B exists because A fails, a "# See also:" at both sites (reason 10 and the docstring). Update the module docstring of ' + LINT + ' in the same change (IFACE item 6): a behaviour change rewrites every doc claim it makes wrong. STOP (ok=false, stop_reason): a file outside the list above; any test edit; a threshold you would have to change; a lint you would have to disable; a test that looks wrong ("test-defect: ..." form).\n' + BRIEF + '\n' + IFACE + '\n' + RULED + '\n' + WHOLE + '\n' + BL + '\nDone when every test of ' + NEWTEST + ' is green with its controls, tests/specfactory fails exactly on the baseline set (test_spec_provenance.py, test_pre_gate.py including :252 and :370, test_rule_pins.py and test_rule_pins_tests.py all green), python -m py_compile is clean on ' + LINT + (PREGATE_EDIT ? ', bash -n is clean on ' + PREGATE_SH : '') + ', and the pre-gate: ' + PREGATE('<worktree>', 'origin/main', NEWTEST) + ' ends PRE_GATE verdict OK; quote it. Report ok, branch, sha, summary (the test lines, every regex and constant you added with its IFACE item), red_ids, parked.', { label: 'build:' + K, phase: 'Build', schema: REPORT, agentType: 'doer', model: 'sonnet' })
const build = await withRuling(mkBuild)
out = { ...out, build }
if (!(build && build.ok)) return { ...out, stopped: 'build:' + K }

phase('Check')
const check = SKIP['check:' + K] ? { pass: true, evidence: 'skipped: check ok' } : await agent(RULES.replace('worktree add -b <branch>', 'worktree add --detach') + '\nRole: gate checker (Engineer), rules.md section (c), read-only, detached worktree at origin/' + build.branch + ' (suffix chk-vg-harness-' + K + '; remove it after with git worktree remove, no --force). Spec: ' + SPEC + '.\n' + BRIEF + '\n' + IFACE + '\n' + RULED + '\n' + WHOLE + '\n' + BL + '\n(1) The diff versus its merge base touches only ' + PRODUCT + ' plus, from the merged test branch, ' + NEWTEST + '; list every other file (blocking)' + (PREGATE_EDIT ? '; the ' + PREGATE_SH + ' diff is the one spec_provenance.py call line gaining --pieces "$PIECES" and nothing else (a dedupe or a header-comment edit is blocking), and ' + TESTPG + ' is untouched' : '; ' + PREGATE_SH + ' unchanged') + '. (2) Run ' + NEWTEST + ', tests/specfactory/test_spec_provenance.py, test_pre_gate.py, test_rule_pins.py, test_rule_pins_tests.py and the whole tests/specfactory: PASS/FAIL per file with counts; the failing set equals the baseline; the rev10 acceptance (at least 39 findings) still holds and no existing test file differs from the base (git diff --name-only on tests/ shows only ' + NEWTEST + '). (3) POSITIVE CONTROLS: in a scratch copy revert ' + PRODUCT + ' to the base: the new red cases go red again for the stated reasons (--pieces rejected with exit 2; the same-unit cited-number cases exit 1 with a (10) finding); list case by case; and today\'s whole-file mode rejects the fixture on both trees. (4) PRE-GATE line format: run ' + PREGATE('<this worktree>', 'origin/main', NEWTEST) + ' and paste EVERY line; each is "PRE_GATE <step> OK|REJECT|WARN ..." (step in noise, gate, tests, pins, provenance, verdict) and it must end PRE_GATE verdict OK; list each WARN (this piece\'s own row has no spec key: a provenance WARN is expected). (5) REAL RUNS (read-only, from this worktree, on its own copies of the specs; locate paragraphs by their bold opening, never by a line number): ' + PY + ' ' + LINT + ' ' + VGSPEC + ' --pieces VG-A-sightdisc; the same with PROTO-scale; with VG-A18-3d; with an id of a bold paragraph the run shows clean (name the id; pick one by running every bold opening id of the spec and listing the zero-finding ones); with a list of two ids; with an id that opens nothing; the same for ' + TSSPEC + ' with HARNESS-cost-report and HARNESS-swarm-config; and the one-argument run on ' + VGSPEC + ' (its count must equal the Preflight whole total minus what the cited-number ruling clears; paste both numbers). Paste for each the exit code, the PROVSCOPE line and the first 12 finding lines. THE AUTHORITY for the counts is the Preflight\'s measurement on the launch tree (whole and ids above); the Doer\'s build must reproduce it: the one-argument run on ' + VGSPEC + ' must give the Preflight\'s cite-reading total and reason-10 count, and each --pieces <id> run must give the Preflight\'s in-scope findings for that id (n and the reasons); a mismatch is blocking true with both numbers. The 600b1831 figures (337 -> 264, reason 10 148 -> 75, VG-A-sightdisc 1 finding (reason 8), PROTO-scale 2 (reasons 3 and 9)) are a labelled comparison only: quote them next to the launch-tree numbers, never as the criterion. DECISIVE FACT, REPORTED not blocking (the Architect\'s input for the records edits): list every row of pieces.toml on this tree that has a spec key, plus VG-A18-3d, HARNESS-csim-xdist, HARNESS-gate-tiers, HARNESS-gate-remote, the gate-speed rows, HARNESS-tool-line, CASCADE-laneU-tests and VG-A-dragbox when they exist, and for EACH run --pieces <id> on its spec and state: exit code, paragraphs=k (k = 0 means it FALLS BACK to the whole file, state that), in-scope findings by reason, the WARN line if any. Expected on the Dispatcher\'s reading of 410990f3, to be confirmed (differences are reported, never blocking): VG-A18-3d falls back (its paragraph opens "A18, ...", not the id); HARNESS-csim-xdist, HARNESS-gate-tiers, HARNESS-gate-remote and the new gate-speed rows have no paragraph on main or one that opens without the id, so they fall back; HARNESS-tool-line and CASCADE-laneU-tests have no paragraph and fall back to the tool-split spec\'s own reason-1 findings; VG-A-dragbox (:411 there) has 3 in-scope findings (reason 3 and reason 10 twice, numbers 4 and 50, no cite); HARNESS-cost-report (list-item opening), HARNESS-swarm-config and the CASCADE row bullet depend on the records edit that tags the tool-split bullets. Also report the shared scope: for each id the paragraphs it matches beyond its own (information: under the paragraph\'s rule a dependency mention in another piece\'s bold opening matches nothing; report any that does), and run --pieces with one matching id and one id that opens nothing: the PROVSCOPE WARN line for the second is printed once and the exit code is that of the matching id; and `--pieces ""` on a real spec. (6) The SPEC PARAGRAPH\'s opening-rule edge cases once more on the real specs: an id named in a bold opening only after the first token (a dependency list: it opens nothing), an id followed by `.` or `**` (`**ID.**`: opens nothing under the paragraph\'s rule; report which real paragraphs open that way), an id in the body only, an id that is a prefix of another id (opens nothing under the longer id), the `- ID` and ``- `ID` `` list-item forms (a bare `- ID` line, end of line as a follower of the plain form, opens a paragraph; the backtick form is closed by its backtick), the last paragraph of the file (no blank line after it). List each of the IFACE item 3 FILLED choices (the list-item followers are in the paragraph now, not a fill) and say whether a real spec paragraph depends on it. (7) Every regex and constant added in the product diff listed with its IFACE item; blocking true for one with no source; the module docstring states the --pieces option, the PROVSCOPE line and the cited-number sentence (stale-doc tripwire), and a grep of the repo (docs/, scripts/, tests/) lists every other claim about spec_provenance.py\'s whole-file behaviour (the HARNESS-provenance paragraph of the visible-game spec at :348, Lane H part 3 at :330, Rev 12c at :358): list them for the records clerk, never edit them. (8) WIRED: state what is reachable after this piece: the ids reach the lint from the pre_gate.sh provenance step on every gate of a spec-keyed row (quote the changed call line and a throwaway-repo run through pre_gate.sh that shows a PROVSCOPE line), or say plainly "stub: the scoping is dormant" if args.pregate is false. Report pass, blocking, evidence (every PASS/FAIL line, every pasted output).', { label: 'check:' + K, phase: 'Check', schema: VERDICT, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' })
out = { ...out, check }
if (!(check && check.pass)) return { ...out, stopped: 'check:' + K }

phase('Clerk')
const clerk = done('clerk:' + K) || await agent((LANDING ? 'LANDING RULE FOR THIS RUN (overrides section (b) where it differs): ' + LANDING + '\n' : '') + RULES + '\nRole: landing clerk (Engineer), rules.md section (b). Piece ' + ROW + ' of ' + SPEC + '; tooling, no shot, no story_reviews row. ' + (PUSH_MAIN ? 'The push to main at the end IS authorised on a clean gate (Westley\'s standing word for clean-gate pushes, passed by the Dispatcher), subject to the known-red rule below. AT MOST ONE LANDING IN FLIGHT: the flock below serialises it.' : 'Do NOT push to main (args.pushMain false): branch only.') + ' DEPENDS CHECK, after git fetch origin and before the lock and before any gate: git show origin/main:docs/northstar/plans/push/pieces.toml, read depends_on of the ' + ROW + ' row and the state of EVERY id in it' + (PREGATE_EDIT ? ' and ALSO the state of HARNESS-C4 (it must be attached on origin/main: this piece owns a line of the file C4 owns)' : '') + '. If any id is not attached on origin/main stop with ok=false, stop_reason "depends-not-attached: <ids>": take no lock, run no gate, land nothing on main, but build, run the tests and the pre-gate and push the branch ' + LB + ' with everything done except the gate, the landing edits and the push to main; write .wt-done; say so at the top of the summary. Branch ' + LB + ', suffix vg-harness-' + K + '-land, from origin/main; merge origin/' + tests.branch + ', origin/' + build.branch + rulingMerge() + '. Stage files by name only; never a *.import or *.uid file; delete untracked .uid files before any checkout or merge. Conflicts: in docs/northstar/plans/push/pieces.toml take origin/main\'s side of every conflicting hunk (the row already carries this piece\'s owns); in ' + LEDGER + ' keep both sides; a row that appears more than once after the merge keeps one copy: drop byte-identical copies; if two copies of a row differ by any byte STOP and report the diff, never pick one. Any other conflict: STOP and report. Run ' + NEWTEST + ' and tests/specfactory (' + PY + ' -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests/specfactory) and list PASS/FAIL per touched file: acceptance tests the gate cannot run for a comma list of pieces (the acceptance-ids and undertest steps WARN and skip: quote the WARN lines); the failing set must equal the baseline (' + ((pre.baseline_red || []).join(', ') || '(none)') + '). Pre-gate before the lock (section (b)): ' + PREGATE('<landing worktree>', 'origin/main', NEWTEST) + '; it must end OK (a lint, footprint, owner-row or noise reject is fixed or reported before the lock, never spent on a full gate). Full gate EXACTLY section (b), detached, from the landing worktree, the lock taken first and origin/main fetched and merged inside it (main moves while a clerk waits for the lock): mkdir -p ~/Projects/om-push/tmp-vg-harness-' + K + '; start in the BACKGROUND: flock -w 14400 ~/Projects/om-push/gate.lock env TMPDIR=$HOME/Projects/om-push/tmp-vg-harness-' + K + ' MERGE_GATE_SUITE_TIMEOUT=2400 MERGE_GATE_PLAYTHROUGH_TIMEOUT=2400 MERGE_GATE_PLAY_TIMEOUT=900 MERGE_GATE_PIECES=<landing worktree>/docs/northstar/plans/push/pieces.toml bash -c \'cd <landing worktree> && git fetch origin && git merge --no-edit origin/main && scripts/specfactory/pre_gate.sh <landing worktree> origin/main ' + PIECES + ' ' + NEWTEST + ' && scripts/specfactory/merge_gate.sh <landing worktree> origin/main ' + PIECES + '\' >$HOME/Projects/om-push/tmp-vg-harness-' + K + '/gate.log 2>&1 (three positional arguments to merge_gate.sh; the last is ONE comma list with no spaces; add any further owner id a footprint line names and re-run the pre-gate; the pre-gate above is the cheap early check and pre_gate runs again inside the lock, on the tree after the merge; the script rejects a candidate that lacks the current origin/main, so a forgotten merge costs seconds, not a gate). Poll gate.log for the ^GATE look line with one foreground command under 10 minutes at a time, every 5 minutes at most; then pgrep -f \'^bash scripts/specfactory/merge_gate.sh\' to confirm no gate for the worktree still runs (never pgrep your own command line). There is no VERDICT line: the verdict is the set of GATE <stage> REJECT lines (and a PRE_GATE REJECT line inside the lock stops the chain: quote it); flake rule per section (b). The push is its OWN command, run only after you have read the verdict from gate.log: never chain git push behind pre_gate.sh or merge_gate.sh in one command line. KNOWN-RED RULE (section (b), Architect 2026-10-12): push main only when EVERY GATE REJECT line names a test or play listed by exact id in scripts/specfactory/gd_tests_known_red.txt or scripts/specfactory/lane_plays_known_red.txt on the landing tree (today: ' + RED_NOW + '); a reject outside those files means branch only, ok=false, stop_reason "gate-reject", every REJECT line quoted, never a push. If no REJECT, or only listed ones: the landing edits are ONE separate RECORDS COMMIT on top of the merged, gated tree (normal prose, ending with the attribution line the conversation gives): in docs/northstar/plans/push/pieces.toml flip ' + ROW + ' to status = { state = "attached", attach_sha = "<sha7 of the gated merge commit, the HEAD before this records commit>" } (the format of the attached rows; comment "landed <sha7>"); ' + LEDGER + ' (PP-ledger): add the rows DRAFT-provscope-forms and DRAFT-provscope-nomatch ONLY if the ledger on the merged tree lacks them (they are on origin/main at push_ledger_2026-09-22.md:1374-1375: when present add nothing, never a second copy); when absent write exactly these two table rows, byte for byte, in the format of the existing rows: ' + LEDGER_FORMS + ' and ' + LEDGER_NOMATCH + '; edit the programme file docs/northstar/plans/2026-10-07-visible-game-programme.md only if its lane table has a row naming ' + ROW + ' (HARNESS-status owns it; else say so); do NOT edit the depends_on of the spec-keyed rows (the records clerk does), the visible-game spec or any doc outside the list (list the stale claims the Check reported in your summary for the records clerk); write nothing about status anywhere else (no ROADMAP lane row, no journal line); no shot, no story_reviews row: this is tooling. Right before the push: git fetch origin; if origin/main moved, merge it in (say so; ledger appends keep both sides) and re-run the pre-gate, not the full gate. Push the branch ' + LB + ', then ' + (PUSH_MAIN ? 'git push origin HEAD:main as its own command (only under the known-red rule above)' : 'stop at the branch (args.pushMain false)') + '. Write .wt-done (date, branch, pushed sha) after the push and remove the worktree only if it is clean and its HEAD is contained in origin (git branch -r --contains HEAD), else leave it with .wt-done; delete only the merge_gate_before_* directories under your own TMPDIR. The report summary carries: the stage lines verbatim ("OK per stage" or every GATE REJECT line), the pre-gate verdict, the WARN lines, the test lines, main head, and the plain statement of what is a stub (every gate of a spec-keyed row now scopes the lint to the paragraphs of the piece ids, WARN lines name unmatched ids; or "dormant" if args.pregate is false). ok=true means landed on main (or the branch under args.pushMain false). Report ok, branch, sha, summary, red_ids, stop_reason.\n' + RULED, { label: 'clerk:' + K, phase: 'Clerk', schema: REPORT, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' })
out = { ...out, clerk }
if (!(clerk && clerk.ok)) return { ...out, stopped: 'clerk:' + K }
return { ...out, pushMain: PUSH_MAIN, pregate: PREGATE_EDIT, next: 'depends_on ' + ROW + ' is already on main for PROTO-scale (pieces.toml:2222), VG-A-sightdisc (:2430), VG-A18-3d (:2445), HARNESS-swarm-config (:3381), HARNESS-tool-line (:3395) and HARNESS-cost-report (:3408), and the spec paragraph is on main (visible-game spec :350), so the records clerk adds only what the Check REAL RUNS show missing (VG-A-dragbox :2454 lists only VG-A-startforce; no CASCADE-P3-trial row exists); the Architect reads the Check REAL RUNS for which pieces still reject at pre_gate; the ledger rows DRAFT-provscope-forms and -nomatch (on main at push_ledger :1374-1375) wait for Westley to confirm' }
